claims:
1. A computing device-implemented method, comprising:
receiving a document;
comparing the document with a prior version of the document;
determining, based on the comparison, at least one first portion of the document that is common with the prior version of the document and at least one second portion of the document that is uncommon with the prior version of the document;
determining an age of the at least one first portion and the at least one second portion;
determining whether the age of the at least one first portion is greater than or equal to an age threshold and that the age of the at least one second portion is less than the age threshold;
calculating a checksum of the document based on the at least one first portion but not the at least one second portion when the age of the at least one first portion is greater than or equal to the age threshold and the age of the at least one second portion is less than the age threshold; and
storing the calculated checksum.

3. The method of claim 1, where determining the age of the at least one first portion and the at least one second portion comprises:
analyzing an age parameter of a token associated with the at least one first portion;
analyzing an age parameter of a token associated with the at least on second portion;
increasing the age parameters each time the document is crawled; and
determining the age of the least one first portion and the at least one second portion based on the increased age parameters.

10. A computing device-implemented system, comprising:
means for receiving an aged version of a document;
means for comparing the aged version of the document with a prior version of the document;
means for determining at least one first portion of the aged version of the document that is common with the prior version of the document based on the comparison;
means for determining at least one second portion of the aged version of the document that is uncommon with the prior version of the document based on the comparison;
means for determining an age of the at least one first portion and the at least one second portion;
means for determining whether the age of the at least one first portion is greater than or equal to an age threshold and that the age of the at least one second portion is less than the age threshold;
means for calculating a checksum of the aged version of the document based on the at least one first portion but not the at least one second portion when the age of the at least one first portion is greater than or equal to the age threshold and the age of the at least one second portion is less than the age threshold;
means for determining whether the calculated checksum matches a checksum associated with a cluster of duplicate documents; and
means for associating the aged version of the document with the cluster of duplicate documents when the calculated checksum matches the checksum associated with the cluster of duplicate documents.

19. A computing device-implemented method, comprising:
receiving a document that includes new content and aged content;
comparing the document with a prior version of the document that includes the aged content but not the new content;
separating the new content and the aged content based on the comparison;
determining ages associated with the new content and the aged content;
determining whether the ages of the new content and the aged content are greater than or equal to an age threshold;
calculating a checksum of the document based on the aged content but not the new content when the age of the aged content is greater than or equal to the age threshold, and the age of the new content is less than the age threshold; and
storing the calculated checksum.

25. A computing device-implemented method, comprising:
receiving, via the computing device, a document that includes new content and aged content;
comparing, via a processor associated with the computing device, the document with a prior version of the document;
determining, via the processor and based on the comparison, the new content that is not in the prior version of the document and the aged content that is in the prior version of the document;
determining, via the processor, ages associated with the new content and the aged content;
determining, via the processor, whether the ages of the new content and the aged content are greater than or equal to an age threshold;
indexing, via the processor, the new content when the age of the new content is determined to be less than the age threshold;
storing the indexed new content in a memory associated with the computing device;
determining, via the processor and when the age of aged content is determined to be greater than or equal to the age threshold, whether the aged content is associated with a cluster of duplicate documents, and
associating, via the processor, the document with the cluster of duplicate documents when the aged content is associated with the cluster of duplicate documents.
